<main class="wrap"><div class="wn-wrap">
  <%- include('partials/home-link') %>
  <div class="page-head"><div><h1 class="page-title">What's new for 17 December</h1><p class="page-sub">The Great War · two weeks, eight nations, one front</p></div></div>
  <% if (!isPublic) { %><div class="wn-draft">Draft: only the owner sees this page until it's made public (site setting whats_new_public). Check every line against the build before publishing.</div><% } %>
  <% if (locals.isOwner) { %><form method="POST" action="/whats-new/public" style="margin:0 0 18px"><input type="hidden" name="public" value="<%= isPublic ? 'off' : 'on' %>"><button type="submit" style="padding:9px 14px;border-radius:10px;border:0;background:<%= isPublic ? 'rgba(255,255,255,.12)' : '#5be38f' %>;color:<%= isPublic ? '#fff' : '#0c1a12' %>;font:800 14px 'Baloo 2',sans-serif;cursor:pointer"><%= isPublic ? 'Back to draft (owner only)' : 'Make this page public' %></button></form><% } %>
  <p class="wn-lead">After the tester event on 21 November, the war comes back bigger. Here is what's new, all of it built on custom-made mods for this event.</p>

  <section class="wn-sec"><h2>The war</h2><div class="wn-grid">
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>War windows</h3><p>Nodes can be taken only in the evening war windows, 19:00 to 22:00 UK time, on a fixed schedule. Outside them the borders are closed, so nobody loses land while asleep. <a href="/great-war-in-2-minutes">The schedule</a></p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>The Christmas Truce</h3><p>On 25 December there is no war window. The guns fall silent along the whole front for the evening.</p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Front-line weather</h3><p>Each war window has its own forecast, rain or light mist, printed in the Daily Front the day before.</p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>After-action reports</h3><p>When a window closes, the paper reports what happened: nodes taken and lost, the fallen, the finest soldiers. In game it's on the War Office's front page.</p></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="wn-sec"><h2>Soldiers</h2><div class="wn-grid">
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Regiments</h3><p>Raise a regiment of 3 to 10 soldiers of your nation with a name, a short tag and a banner. Its tag shows next to your name, and it can be mentioned in dispatches.</p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Daily orders</h3><p>Three small orders a day from what your nation needs: stand guard, fortify a node, cook rations, or fight while at war. Paid, with a bonus for days in a row.</p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Medics are paid</h3><p>A Medic can now treat a wounded comrade with a bandage or kit, and is paid for healing the wounds the enemy dealt.</p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Gallantry medals</h3><p>Each nation's Leader can award a few gallantry medals a week, each with a citation, shown on the uniform and the service record.</p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>A fair start for late joiners</h3><p>From day 5 a new soldier starts near his nation's rank, never above Corporal, so nobody joins as a Private facing Lieutenants.</p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Uniforms that show it</h3><p>Your uniform wears with every day you survive: clean on your first, battered after a week. Rank and medals show on it too.</p></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="wn-sec"><h2>Remembrance</h2><div class="wn-grid">
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Dog tags and memorials</h3><p>Every fallen soldier drops his army's dog tag. Bring your own side's tags to your capital's memorial and the names are carved there. Enemy tags are trophies.</p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Death recap</h3><p>When you fall you see who got you, with what and from how far, and how your life went.</p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Field post and trench art</h3><p>(Being built.) Write field postcards to your comrades, and turn spent shell cases into trench art that keeps your name.</p></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="wn-sec"><h2>Supply and trade</h2><div class="wn-grid">
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Rations and the field kitchen</h3><p>Each army has its own rations, cooked at a field kitchen from farm food. A good meal keeps your stamina up.</p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Life after death</h3><p>Soldiers whose army can't bring them back (it has fallen, or lost its capital) can write for the Daily Front as war correspondents (their dispatches run once the war window they cover has closed), and call the front in the front-line wager: who holds each contested node when the window closes. <a href="/wager">The table</a></p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>The market board</h3><p>See what every nation's stalls are selling, and for how much, on the website. <a href="/market">The market</a></p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Winter kit</h3><p>Greatcoats, balaclavas and gloves for every army, for the December cold.</p></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="wn-sec"><h2>On the website</h2><div class="wn-grid">
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Your night, as a card</h3><p>After each window, a card of what you did, ready to share on Discord. <a href="/soldier">Service records</a></p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>Call to the line</h3><p>Turn it on in the War Office and you get a Discord message when one of your nation's nodes is under attack and you're not online. Never at night your time.</p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>The War Office on your phone</h3><p>Orders, jobs, mail and the front, wherever you are. <a href="/war-office">The War Office</a></p></div>
    <div class="wn-item"><h3>New players</h3><p>A Field Service Pocket Book in game, and <a href="/first-hour">your first hour</a> and <a href="/pack-faq">the modpack FAQ</a> here.</p></div>
  </div></section>

  <p class="wn-foot">Numbers may still change before 17 December. <a href="/wiki">The Field Manual</a> has the details.</p>
</div></main>
